====================================================================
  ACS CORP — RISK TIMELINE QUICK REFERENCE
  For use with Vulnerability Report Form and Remediation Tickets
====================================================================

REMEDIATION SLA BY SEVERITY (from ACS-POL-SI-002):
----------------------------------------------------
  Critical (9.0-10.0):   7 calendar days from discovery
  High (7.0-8.9):       14 calendar days from discovery
  Medium (4.0-6.9):     30 calendar days from discovery
  Low (0.1-3.9):        90 calendar days from discovery

DEADLINE CALCULATION EXAMPLES:
-------------------------------
  Discovery: Jun 1   | CVSS 9.3 Critical | Deadline: Jun 8
  Discovery: Jun 1   | CVSS 7.5 High     | Deadline: Jun 15
  Discovery: Jun 1   | CVSS 5.0 Medium   | Deadline: Jul 1
  Discovery: Jun 1   | CVSS 2.1 Low      | Deadline: Aug 30

ROUTING GUIDE:
--------------
  Severity      Primary Owner         Escalation
  ---------------------------------------------------------------
  Critical      IT Admin (immediate)  CISO within 24 hours
  High          IT Admin (scheduled)  Compliance Officer at SLA-3
  Medium        System Owner          IT Admin at SLA-7
  Low           System Owner          Routine review cycle

EXCEPTION PROCESS:
------------------
  - Risk acceptance requires VP-level written approval
  - Must document compensating controls
  - Maximum acceptance: 90 days (one renewal permitted)
  - Critical findings with active exploits: NO exceptions allowed

COMPLIANCE NOTES:
-----------------
  - "In progress" does NOT equal "remediated"
  - Failed patch attempts do NOT stop the SLA clock
  - SLA measured from DISCOVERY date, not ticket creation date
  - Compliance = confirmed resolution via re-scan

====================================================================
Reference: NIST SP 800-53 SI-2, CMMC SI.L1-3.14.1
